  "solution": {
    "text": "$S=(2+\\sqrt{3})^8$\nFor sum of rational terms\n$\\begin{aligned} & ={ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_0(2)^8+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_2(2)^6 \\cdot(\\sqrt{3})^2+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_4(2)^4(\\sqrt{3})^4 \\\\ & \\quad+\\quad{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_6(2)^2(\\sqrt{3})^6+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_8(\\sqrt{3})^8 \\\\ & =2^8+28 \\times 2^6 \\cdot 3+70.2^4 \\cdot 9+28.2^2 .27+81 \\\\ & =256+5376+10080+3024+81 \\\\ & =18817\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
